---
const site = "https://irchad.chat/";
const title = "Delete your account · IrChad";
const description = "How to delete your IrChad account and its data, what is deleted and what is kept.";
---
<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
  <meta charset="utf-8" />
  <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1" />
  <title>{title}</title>
  <link rel="icon" href="/favicon.svg" type="image/svg+xml" />
  <meta name="description" content={description} />
  <link rel="canonical" href={`${site}delete-account`} />
</head>
<body>
  <main>
    <p><a href="/">← IrChad</a></p>
    <h1>Delete your IrChad account</h1>
    <p class="muted">IrChad is a client: your account lives on the network (server) you signed up on, not with the IrChad developer.
      Deleting it removes it from that network. The steps are the same on every IrChad network.</p>

    <h2>Steps</h2>
    <h3>Android</h3>
    <ol>
      <li>Open the network, then tap your name or avatar to open <b>Your status and profile</b>.</li>
      <li>Tap <b>Leave &lt;network&gt;…</b>.</li>
      <li>Tick <b>Delete account</b>, then tap <b>Delete and leave</b>.</li>
    </ol>
    <h3>iOS</h3>
    <ol>
      <li>Open <b>Settings</b>, find the network in the list and tap <b>Leave</b>.</li>
      <li>Tap <b>Delete account and leave</b>.</li>
    </ol>
    <h3>Linux and Windows</h3>
    <ol>
      <li>Click the <b>⋯</b> menu next to the network's name in the sidebar and choose <b>Leave network…</b>.</li>
      <li>Tick <b>Delete account</b> and confirm.</li>
    </ol>
    <h3>Without the app</h3>
    <ol>
      <li>Connect to the network with any IRC client and log in to your account.</li>
      <li>Send <code>/msg NickServ UNREGISTER &lt;account&gt;</code>.</li>
      <li>NickServ replies with a confirmation command containing a code. Send it as shown, e.g. <code>/msg NickServ UNREGISTER &lt;account&gt; &lt;code&gt;</code>.</li>
    </ol>
    <p>If you can't log in any more, ask that network's operator to delete the account for you.
      For the official IrChad server, email <a href="mailto:android@irchad.chat">android@irchad.chat</a> from the address you signed up with, and include your account name.</p>

    <h2>What is deleted</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Your account: its password and the email address you signed up with.</li>
      <li>Everything the network stores with your account: your display name, avatar, status and the public keys used for encrypted DMs.</li>
      <li>Channels you founded lose their registration.</li>
      <li><b>Your messages</b> in channels and DMs are removed from the network's history. Channel messages also disappear for people who are online, and IrChad apps remove their saved copies the next time they connect.</li>
      <li><b>Files you uploaded</b>, including your avatar.</li>
      <li>On the device you used, the app forgets the network, your saved password and your DM encryption keys.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>What is kept</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><b>Your account name</b> stays reserved, so nobody can sign up as you later. Nothing else is stored with it.</li>
      <li><b>Copies other people already saved</b> in apps other than IrChad, such as other IRC clients and bouncers, and DMs already on the other person's devices. The network can't reach into those.</li>
      <li><b>Server logs</b>, such as connection records, follow the operator's own retention policy.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>Deleting your account with an IrChad app does this cleanup. Deleting it from another IRC client (the steps above) removes only the account, so email us for the rest.
      For the official IrChad server, email <a href="mailto:android@irchad.chat">android@irchad.chat</a> to have your remaining messages and files removed.
      We do this within 30 days. See the <a href="/privacy">privacy policy</a> for more.</p>
  </main>
</body>
</html>

<style is:global>
  /* The same Catppuccin tokens as privacy.astro. */
  :root { color-scheme: light dark; --bg: #e6e9ef; --fg: #4c4f69; --muted: #6c6f85; --accent: #40a02b; }
  @media (prefers-color-scheme: dark) { :root { --bg: #11111b; --fg: #cdd6f4; --muted: #a6adc8; --accent: #a6e3a1; } }
  * { box-sizing: border-box; }
  body { margin: 0; background: var(--bg); color: var(--fg); font: 16px/1.6 system-ui, sans-serif; }
  main { max-width: 44rem; margin: 0 auto; padding: 2rem 16px 4rem; }
  a { color: inherit; text-decoration-color: var(--accent); }
  a:focus-visible { outline: 2px solid var(--accent); outline-offset: 2px; }
  h1 { font-size: 2.25rem; margin: 1rem 0 0; }
  h2 { font-size: 1.3rem; margin: 2.5rem 0 .5rem; }
  h3 { font-size: 1.05rem; margin: 1.25rem 0 0; }
  .muted { color: var(--muted); }
  li { margin: .35rem 0; }
  code { font-size: .9em; overflow-wrap: anywhere; }
</style>
